Devices:- 3 Routers: R0, ISP (R1), R2 (1941)
Connections:
- R0 connects to ISP R1.
- ISP R1 connects to R2.
- A virtual GRE tunnel connects R0 directly to R2.
 CONNECT THOURGH COPPER WIRE

! On Router0:
interface gig0/0
ip address 1.1.1.1 255.0.0.0
no shutdown
interface lo 0
ip address 10.1.1.1 255.255.255.0
no shutdown
exit

! On Router1:
interface gig0/0
ip address 1.1.1.2 255.0.0.0
no shutdown
interface gig0/1
ip address 2.2.2.1 255.0.0.0
no shutdown
interface lo 0
ip address 20.1.1.1 255.255.255.0
no shutdown
exit
hostname ISP

! On Router2:
interface gig0/1
 ip address 2.2.2.2 255.0.0.0
 no shutdown
interface lo 0
 ip address 30.1.1.1 255.255.255.0
 no shutdown
 exit


 Add Static Routes Through ISP
 ! On Router0:
ip route 2.0.0.0 255.0.0.0 1.1.1.2
! On Router2:
ip route 1.0.0.0 255.0.0.0 2.2.2.1


Configure GRE Tunnel 1 on Both Endpoints
! On Router0:
configure terminal
interface tunnel 1
 tunnel source gig0/0
 tunnel destination 2.2.2.2
 ip address 192.168.13.1 255.255.255.0
 no shutdown
 end

! On Router2:
configure terminal
interface tunnel 1
 tunnel source gig0/1
 tunnel destination 1.1.1.1
 ip address 192.168.13.3 255.255.255.0
 no shutdown
 end

Test Connectivity Across the GRE Tunnel
 ! On Router0:
ping 192.168.13.3
! On Router2:
ping 192.168.13.1
